1
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,290
And the next wedding gift is

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,660
a gravy boat.

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,740
Ooh, one gravy boat.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:10,880
That's from Sheldon.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,310
He told me he had it engraved.

6
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,190
"In the event of a divorce,

7
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:16,700
please return to Sheldon Cooper."

8
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:20,110
One "Inappropriate,

9
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:23,680
yet I wish I thought of that" gravy boat.

10
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,370
When I get married I'm going to register

11
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:27,360
at the UCLA Cadaver Lab.

12
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,210
Ew, why?

13
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,910
'Cause I've always wanted a whole human skeleton

14
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:33,140
and they are really spendy.

15
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:37,420
So, you actually see you and Sheldon getting married someday?

16
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,760
Not just someday.

17
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,700
In exactly four years.

18
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,710
But don't tell Sheldon.

19
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:43,630
He's still a flight risk.

20
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,200
What about you, Penny?

21
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,090
What about me what?

22
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:50,780
Do you think you and Leonard might ever get married?

23
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:54,100
Oh, well, you know,

24
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,430
Leonard is great.

25
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,710
But do you think you'll ever get married?

26
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:01,340
He's a sweetie.

27
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:04,060
You're not answering the question.

28
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:05,100
Do you love him?

29
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:07,700
Yeah, sure, of course I love him.

30
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:08,870
It doesn't sound like it.

31
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:09,930
Well, I do.

32
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:12,790
Do you tell him that?

33
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:15,710
No, he'd just take it the wrong way.

34
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,150
What does that mean?

35
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:20,980
It means he is special and smart and nice and...

36
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:23,160
- Are you gonna break up with him? - No!

37
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,230
Maybe. I don't know.

38
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:27,090
I had no idea you were unhappy.

39
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:28,140
That's the thing: I'm not.

40
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,810
I'm not unhappy at all. It's just... I don't know...

41
00:01:30,810 --> 00:01:33,990
I-I've been in love before, but it felt different.

42
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:38,470
But maybe this is a new, better, boring kind of love.

43
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:41,640
Do you ever feel that way about Howard?

44
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,530
Oh, that's not really a fair comparison.

45
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:46,450
I'm basically married to a sexy Buzz Lightyear.

46
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:49,600
Amy, you?

47
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:50,590
Can't help ya, kid.

48
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,750
Whenever I'm around Sheldon,

49
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:53,920
I feel like my loins are on fire.

50
00:01:55,270 --> 00:01:56,180
In the good way.

51
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:58,740
Not the urinary tract infection way.

52
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:29,570
Hey, buddy, how's it going up there?

53
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,620
You don't have to shout, Raj.

54
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:35,300
It's not like I'm an astronaut floating around in outer space.

55
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,180
Oh, wait, I am.

56
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:44,100
So, is it everything you hoped it would be?

57
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,340
It's better.

58
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:49,160
I wake up every morning and I just can't believe

59
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,550
I'm on this incredible adventure.

60
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:52,640
Hey, Froot Loops,

61
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,610
did you clean the space toilet?

62
00:02:57,070 --> 00:02:59,570
Excuse me. I'm talking to my friends.

63
00:02:59,570 --> 00:03:03,300
You know the rules: new guy scrubs the toilet.

64
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,310
If you do good job, next time we give you brush.

65
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:13,610
Funny.

66
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:17,150
We're always giving each other a hard time up here.

67
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:18,750
It's kind of like being in a frat.

68
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:23,090
You know, joking, kidding around, hurting feelings.

69
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:24,890
Okay, my turn. Let me talk to him.

70
00:03:24,890 --> 00:03:26,040
Go ahead.

71
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,090
2311 North Los Robles Avenue,

72
00:03:28,090 --> 00:03:31,330
Pasadena, California to International Space Station.

73
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:32,760
Can you read me? Over.

74
00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:37,200
Yes, I read you, Sheldon.

75
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,590
Copy that. Over.

76
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,200
What are you doing?

77
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,200
I am talking to a man in space.

78
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,430
If you don't have the

79
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:47,460
then he might as well be at the Coffee Bean over on Lake Street.

80
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:49,990
You're out of your mind, Sheldon.

81
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:53,120
That's a negative. My mother had me tested. Over.

82
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:56,460
Come on, scrub it up, Loops.

83
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,840
All right, all right.

84
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,180
I gotta go.

85
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:02,560
There's a meteor shower.

86
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,520
You want to see a meteor shower?

87
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,550
Take a look at what Dimitri just left you in the toilet.

88
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,670
Bye.

89
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,950
Over and out.

90
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,820
Bye, buddy!

91
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,340
Hello.

92
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:21,450
Hey, Stuart, come on in.

93
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:22,700
What are you doing here?

94
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,650
Um, Raj invited me to go to the movies with you guys.

95
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:28,450
Excuse me.

96
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:31,270
I didn't authorize this.

97
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:34,340
Sheldon, you are not in charge.

98
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:35,990
That's mighty sassy for a man

99
00:04:35,990 --> 00:04:38,650
with a roommate performance review around the corner.

100
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,760
What's the big deal?

101
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,380
You guys are bringing your girlfriends.

102
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,990
The big deal is I was expecting us

103
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,930
to be an intimate group of five.

104
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:49,440
Now, we're going to be a...

105
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,580
faceless mass of six.

106
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:55,940
It'll be fine. Just, uh, pretend he's Wolowitz.

107
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,610
Do you like Raisinets?

108
00:05:02,610 --> 00:05:03,570
I can take them or leave them.

109
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:06,070
At the movies, Wolowitz always eats Raisinets.

110
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:08,650
Would you feel more comfortable if I ate Raisinets?

111
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:11,140
Well, it's hardly my business what you eat,

112
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,180
as long as it doesn't crunch during the film

113
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,750
and it's Raisinets.

114
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:17,600
Okay.

115
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,390
Should we go?

116
00:05:18,390 --> 00:05:19,700
Yeah, but, one more question.

117
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:20,940
If you're going to replace Wolowitz,

118
00:05:20,970 --> 00:05:22,260
I need to know a little more about you.

119
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:22,970
All right.

120
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:24,910
Wolowitz went to MIT.

121
00:05:24,910 --> 00:05:26,540
What's your educational background?

122
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:28,210
I went to art school.

123
00:05:28,210 --> 00:05:29,740
Equally ridiculous. Let's go.

124
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:55,230
This insistence on hand-holding is preposterous.

125
00:05:56,150 --> 00:05:57,210
Well, I like it.

126
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:57,970
Yeah, of course you do.

127
00:05:57,970 --> 00:06:01,870
You're a girl. You like all kinds of hippy-dippy things.

128
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,620
Just watch the movie.

129
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,060
It's not fair.

130
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:11,650
Penny isn't making Leonard hold hands.

131
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:15,700
There might be a reason for that.

132
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,240
Sweaty?

133
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,780
Unhygienic?

134
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,010
Looks dumb?

135
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:22,270
Take your pick.

136
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:25,120
Penny said she's not sure

137
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,320
she wants to be Leonard's girlfriend anymore.

138
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:34,530
Wrong. She just took a sip from his Diet Dr. Pepper.

139
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:36,710
So?

140
00:06:36,710 --> 00:06:39,180
So, if she wants to end her pair-bond with Leonard,

141
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:41,270
why on earth would she guzzle a witches' brew

142
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:43,090
of his soda and spit?

143
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,590
It's complicated.

144
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:48,910
String theory is complicated.

145
00:06:50,170 --> 00:06:51,700
That's just yucky.

146
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,060
Don't get any ideas.

147
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,750
All right, for the sake of argument, let's say that's true.

148
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:05,310
Why doesn't Penny just end the relationship?

149
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:07,540
She's not sure how she feels.

150
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:10,290
How can she not be sure how she feels?

151
00:07:10,290 --> 00:07:12,600
You know, when I have a feeling, I know it.

152
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:15,330
Trains? Love them.

153
00:07:16,570 --> 00:07:18,690
Swordfish? I love them, too.

154
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:22,170
They're fish with a sword for a nose.

155
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:28,090
Regardless, don't say anything to Leonard.

156
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,560
Now you're asking me to keep a secret

157
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:33,180
from my best friend, colleague, and roommate?

158
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:35,490
Yes, please, Penny will kill me.

159
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:37,060
Fine.

160
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:40,590
FYI, secret-keeping? Hate it.

161
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:43,720
Hand-holding? Not a fan.

162
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:47,800
Hammerhead shark? I love that thing.

163
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:51,790
Yeah, it's another fish with a tool on its head.

164
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,440
Raisinet?

165
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,610
Shh, we're trying to watch the movie.

166
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:01,670
This is not working out with him.

167
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:18,080
What are you doing?

168
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,940
I think I might have tartar buildup.

169
00:08:22,850 --> 00:08:25,440
My tongue won't go as far forward as it used to.

170
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:29,130
Maybe your tongue is shrinking.

171
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,670
Nope.

172
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:45,140
Oh, you have no idea how annoying this is.

173
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:48,770
I'm starting to get a sense of it.

174
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:53,460
Don't worry. I'll take you to the dentist tomorrow.

175
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:54,910
Thank you.

176
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:57,100
I appreciate that.

177
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:59,230
You're good people, Leonard.

178
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,730
There's something I need to tell you.

179
00:09:09,730 --> 00:09:10,740
Okay.

180
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:14,090
I can't tell you.

181
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,580
Why?

182
00:09:18,130 --> 00:09:20,310
I can't tell you why I can't tell you.

183
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:24,420
So I guess there's two things I can't tell you.

184
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,790
I wish there were more.

185
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:29,760
Good night.

186
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:37,680
I'm sorry.

187
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,650
- This is really important. - What is it?

188
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:45,240
I like The Transformers.

189
00:09:46,930 --> 00:09:49,310
Do you like The Transformers?

190
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:52,950
Where exactly did your mother have you tested?

191
00:09:53,990 --> 00:09:55,430
Leonard,

192
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,000
The Transformers teach us

193
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,350
that things are not always what they appear to be.

194
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,890
You know, like, uh,

195
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:06,570
a semi truck might be an alien robot,

196
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:11,340
or, uh, someone in a romantic relationship, uh, might feel

197
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,530
differently than they appear to.

198
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:15,850
Or a conversation

199
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:18,720
about The Transformers might actually be

200
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:21,140
about someone in this room.

201
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:29,160
I'm going to pause to let that sink in.

202
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:33,970
- Okay, I think I understand. - You do?

203
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:39,250
The guy who seems like an emotionless robot is you...

204
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:45,330
but your relationship with Amy is causing you to transform

205
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:49,150
into a red-blooded man with sexual desires.

206
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,830
That is literally the stupidest thing I've ever heard.

207
00:11:05,530 --> 00:11:06,120
Leonard?

208
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,730
Leonard.

209
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:09,260
Leonard?

210
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:11,190
What?

211
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,500
Are you sleeping?

212
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:16,420
I was. Now I'm having a nightmare.

213
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:19,530
What do you want?

214
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:23,860
Never mind. I still can't tell you.

215
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:28,790
Penny?

216
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,280
Penny.

217
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:41,460
Penny.

218
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:46,490
Oh, my God.

219
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:47,340
Sheldon?

220
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,520
You frightened me.

221
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:55,490
What are you doing in my bedroom?

222
00:11:55,490 --> 00:11:56,890
Yeah, well, I knocked on the front door,

223
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,090
but you didn't hear it.

224
00:11:58,090 --> 00:12:00,330
How did you even get in, you weirdo?

225
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:01,530
Yeah, really?

226
00:12:01,530 --> 00:12:03,990
I've seen strange men traipsing in and out of here for years,

227
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,160
but when I do it, it's weird?

228
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,100
What do you want, Sheldon?

229
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,550
Oh, I was having a little trouble sleeping

230
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:12,710
and I just thought,

231
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:15,370
uh, seeing as you're up, we could talk.

232
00:12:16,710 --> 00:12:17,810
Talk about what?

233
00:12:17,810 --> 00:12:19,110
Oh, I don't know.

234
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:23,520
Uh, weather, uh, fish you could do carpentry with.

235
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,850
Why Leonard is such an attractive

236
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:27,420
and desirable boyfriend.

237
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,410
Yeah, pick one-- your choice.

238
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:31,170
Sheldon.

239
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:33,890
Did you know that Leonard has a perfect driving record

240
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:37,380
and enjoys the insurance discounts that go along with that?

241
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:38,790
Hubba-hubba.

242
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:43,450
- Okay, go home, crazy man. - Yeah.

243
00:12:43,450 --> 00:12:45,220
Did you know that

244
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:48,080
while Leonard is not considered a tall fellow in our country,

245
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:51,350
in today's North Korea, he's downright average.

246
00:12:52,150 --> 00:12:54,060
Talk about a keeper.

247
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:57,420
Okay, what did Amy tell you?

248
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,730
Oh, very well.

249
00:12:58,730 --> 00:13:01,260
I can't keep up this clever charade any longer.

250
00:13:02,570 --> 00:13:03,680
She told me

251
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:06,030
that you were thinking of ending it with Leonard.

252
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,220
Okay, you listen to me.

253
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,720
I think it's really sweet you're trying to protect your friend,

254
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,730
but this is none of your business. Got it?

255
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:16,310
Excuse me. This is not about protecting my friend.

256
00:13:20,510 --> 00:13:24,070
I'm a big fan of homeostasis.

257
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:25,360
Do you know what that is?

258
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,950
- Of course not. - Yeah.

259
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:31,830
Homeostasis refers to a system's ability

260
00:13:31,830 --> 00:13:33,920
to regulate its internal environment

261
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:36,660
and maintain a constant condition of properties

262
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:38,920
like temperature or pH.

263
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,740
Worst bedtime story ever.

264
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:45,730
My point is

265
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:47,520
I don't like when things change.

266
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:49,910
So, regardless of your feelings,

267
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:52,370
I would like you to continue dating Leonard.

268
00:13:53,690 --> 00:13:54,640
And also,

269
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:57,280
while we're on the subject, you recently changed your shampoo.

270
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:59,700
I'm not comfortable with the new scent.

271
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:03,420
Please stop this madness and go back to green apple.

272
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:07,570
Okay, honey, I have a lot to figure out,

273
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:11,020
and until I do, you are not to say a word to Leonard.

274
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,610
- Do you understand? - I do.

275
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:16,530
- You clear on the shampoo issue? - Get out.

276
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,960
- Penny? - What?

277
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:26,720
Please don't hurt my friend.

278
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:31,070
- That is the last thing I want to do. - Thank you.

279
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,140
Coconut? What were you thinking?

280
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:37,810
- Are you a hula girl? - Get out!

281
00:14:46,410 --> 00:14:47,370
Hello?

282
00:14:47,370 --> 00:14:49,780
What the hell is wrong with you? You told Sheldon?

283
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,990
Do you know what a terrible position this puts me in?

284
00:14:53,030 --> 00:14:55,130
Hang on, please.

285
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,590
Hello?

286
00:14:57,590 --> 00:14:59,050
Yeah, just a heads-up:

287
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:01,080
Penny knows that you blabbed about Leonard.

288
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,590
She's pretty mad.

289
00:15:04,230 --> 00:15:04,800
I know.

290
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,720
She's yelling at me right now.

291
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:09,880
All right then, so we're all on the same page.

292
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:12,060
Yeah.

293
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,670
Hey, Bernie.

294
00:15:16,670 --> 00:15:18,010
There's my hubby.

295
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:19,640
How's everything going up there?

296
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:21,400
Oh, it's okay.

297
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,670
Space is beautiful.

298
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:26,000
Earth is beautiful. Same old, same old.

299
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:30,030
- What's wrong? - Nothing.

300
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:31,420
Everything's fine.

301
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:32,930
Howard.

302
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:38,570
The other astronauts are being mean to me.

303
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:42,910
No, what are they doing?

304
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:45,980
Well, like for instance, the other day when I was asleep,

305
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:49,590
one of the guys went on a space walk

306
00:15:49,590 --> 00:15:54,470
and glued a big-eyed rubber alien mask to the outside of my window.

307
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:58,310
When I woke up, I screamed for like nine minutes.

308
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,080
Oh, Howie.

309
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,350
You can see it if you want. It's on YouTube.

310
00:16:03,350 --> 00:16:05,970
Google "Astronaut screams for nine minutes."

311
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:10,160
Why don't you stand up to them?

312
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:12,400
What am I supposed to say?

313
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,040
I don't know.

314
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:16,800
Say, "Being mean is lame.

315
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:19,260
What's cool is being nice."

316
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:28,700
Great, I'll do that when I want to be the first guy

317
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,580
in space to get a wedgie.

318
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,710
Do you want me to call somebody at NASA?

319
00:16:34,710 --> 00:16:36,200
No.

320
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,430
My mom already tried that.

321
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:39,140
It only made things worse.

322
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:44,310
Gelatinous Sphere.

323
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,000
Focused Locust.

324
00:16:47,570 --> 00:16:49,020
Temple of Yip.

325
00:16:49,970 --> 00:16:52,700
I'm sorry. Wolowitz would never play that card.

326
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,790
All right, Lesser Demon Turtle.

327
00:16:57,790 --> 00:16:59,920
Fairy God Monster, I win.

328
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:04,040
Your desperate need for friendship makes you weak.

329
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,730
So, what are you guys doing later?

330
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:10,300
Stuart and I were thinking of going out for a drink.

331
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:11,690
We're gonna try to meet some girls.

332
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:13,470
'Cause that's what we do.

333
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:16,160
Watch out, ladies:

334
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,370
a little coffee and cream coming your way.

335
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:24,340
In case you didn't follow that, I'm the coffee.

336
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,510
Leonard?

337
00:17:27,510 --> 00:17:30,380
Maybe you'd like to go with them to meet girls.

338
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:32,560
Why would I be interested? I have Penny.

339
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,550
Yeah, for now.

340
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:38,120
But that woman has a death wish, Leonard.

341
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:42,360
She talks to strangers; she pets unfamiliar dogs;

342
00:17:42,370 --> 00:17:44,740
and it is ridiculously easy

343
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:46,750
to break into her apartment.

344
00:17:47,710 --> 00:17:49,030
If I were you,

345
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:50,280
I'd get a back-up.

346
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,810
You can't just replace someone you care about

347
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:54,730
with some other random person.

348
00:17:54,730 --> 00:17:57,380
No, please don't ruin this for me.

349
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:02,170
Do you remember how upset I was

350
00:18:02,170 --> 00:18:05,150
when they replaced Edward Norton as the Hulk?

351
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:07,630
Yes, you walked around for a week saying,

352
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:10,290
"Sheldon unhappy with casting choice."

353
00:18:11,950 --> 00:18:15,960
But, then Mark Ruffalo was the Hulk in The Avengers,

354
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,650
and he was even better.

355
00:18:17,650 --> 00:18:18,640
What's your point?

356
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,170
Call me a romantic.

357
00:18:20,170 --> 00:18:22,000
I like to think

358
00:18:22,010 --> 00:18:25,390
that your Mark Ruffalo is still out there somewhere.

359
00:18:27,190 --> 00:18:29,510
This is ridiculous. Are we gonna play cards or not?

360
00:18:30,030 --> 00:18:31,560
I like Mark Ruffalo, too.

361
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:33,580
Yeah, settle down there, Fake Wolowitz.

362
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,690
No one likes a kiss-up.

363
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:43,290
So, I had to take Sheldon to the dentist this morning.

364
00:18:43,930 --> 00:18:45,430
- Really? - Yup.

365
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:47,500
I told him if he didn't bite the hygienist,

366
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:49,170
I'd take him for ice cream.

367
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,340
I didn't have to take him for ice cream.

368
00:18:56,310 --> 00:18:57,090
You okay?

369
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:58,440
You seem a little distracted.

370
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:04,670
Look, there's something I need to tell you.

371
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:07,500
Yeah, okay.

372
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:09,270
I don't really know how to say this.

373
00:19:09,270 --> 00:19:10,710
Just say it.

374
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:13,700
Okay. Here goes.

375
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:22,850
You slept with him?

376
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,470
I didn't know what else to do.

377
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:27,840
He had those big, sad eyes.

378
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:30,030
Oh, sure, you had no choice.

379
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,650
He looked at me like this.

380
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:40,350
Well, if that's all it takes,

381
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:42,200
it's a good thing you don't have a dog.

382
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:47,450
Don't worry.

383
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:49,700
You'll have plenty of chances to break up with him:

384
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:51,180
Your wedding day, your honeymoon,

385
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,950
your 50th anniversary.

386
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,720
Look, it's fine.

387
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:56,310
We're not getting married, okay?

388
00:19:56,310 --> 00:20:00,100
We're keeping things, you know, homeostasis.

389
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:04,370
It's so cute when she tries.

390
00:20:10,350 --> 00:20:11,710
It's from Leonard.

391
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,230
"Last night was amazing.

392
00:20:13,230 --> 00:20:14,260
You're amazing.

393
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:17,050
I'm so lucky to have you in my life."

394
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:21,410
Okay, stop it.

395
00:20:26,430 --> 00:20:27,890
Hey, Bernie, guess what?

396
00:20:27,890 --> 00:20:30,150
I stood up to the other astronauts like you said

397
00:20:30,150 --> 00:20:32,900
and I got to tell you, last night was the first time

398
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:35,310
in a week I got a good night's sleep.

399
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:44,520
Oh, Howie.

400
00:20:45,830 --> 00:20:47,650
What's wrong? You look upset.

401
00:20:47,650 --> 00:20:51,340
Nope, this is my proud face.

